b definitions), \S3.6.1 (Load Resource participation), \S3.10.7.3 (incl.\ (1)(c)) and \S3.10.7.3.1, \S3.14.3.1 (ERS procurement: (1) the four ERS Standard Contract Terms; (2) the four ERS service types, weather-sensitive and non-weather-sensitive ERS-10 and ERS-30; (3) and (11)(b) offers only from QSEs capable of XML messaging, on the written authorization of the Entity controlling the resource; (8) minimum capacity offer 0.1 MW, or 0.5 MW for an ERS Load on the weather-sensitive baseline, with aggregation permitted to reach it; (11)(f) no offered capacity committed to any other product, service or program, incl.\ Ancillary Services, SCED and TDSP standard offer programs; (17)(b) 24 hours of cumulative deployment time per ERS Contract Period in the December--March term and 12 hours in all others; (22) deployment brings no additional payment), \S3.16--3.18 (AS quantities, limits, and offer rules), \S4.4.11 (offer caps, Emergency Pricing Program, PNM threshold \$315,000 per MW-year), \S4.5.2(2) (ERCOT posts hourly DAM results, incl.\ MCPCs, DASPPs and Day-Ahead hourly LMPs, no later than 1330), \S4.6.2.2 (Day-Ahead Energy Charge), \S6.3.2(2) (Real-Time operations timeline: the LMPs for each Resource Node, Load Zone and Hub are posted immediately subsequent to deployment of Base Points and Ancillary Service awards from SCED, ``with the time stamp the prices are effective''; Settlement Point Prices immediately following the end of each Settlement Interval), \S6.4.9.1.1 (Real-Time AS awards), \S6.5.5.2 and \S6.5.7.4 (Load Resource telemetry; SCED Base Points over ICCP), \S6.5.9.4.1(2) (ERCOT may deploy contracted ERS-10 and ERS-30 when PRC falls below 3,000 MW and is not projected to recover above 3,000 MW within 30 minutes following the deployment of Non-Spin; a general procedure prior to EEA operations), \S6.6.1 and \S6.6.3.2 (Real-Time Settlement Point Prices; energy imbalance at a Load Zone, incl.\ (1)(h)), \S6.6.1.1 (Real-Time Settlement Point Price at a Resource Node, floored at $-$\$251/MWh), \S6.6.1.2(1) (Load Zone price, with no reserve adder), \S6.6.3.8, \S8.1.1 (Load Resource AS qualification, testing and performance, incl.\ the two-failure rule, which excludes CLRs, the sustain durations and CLR base-point performance), \S8.1.3 (ERS performance evaluation: availability factors, payment reductions and suspension), \S8.4(2), \S8.5.2.1 (with its NPRR1244 gray box), \S9.16.1 and \S10.3.2.3 (generation netting, effective 1 June 2026), \S9.17.1 (4CP peak determination; NPRR1188 gray boxes), \S11.1.6(4) (NPRR1188 gray box on 4CP), \S10.2.3 and \S10.9 (settlement metering for Load Resources; \S10.9.1(2)(h) and \S10.9.2(1)(h) divide each hour into Settlement Intervals ending at XX:15, XX:30, XX:45 and XX:00), \S13 (loss factors applied to metered Load), \S16.2.1, \S16.2.3.2(1) (a Resource Entity as its own QSE), \S16.3.1.1(1) (LSE designation of a QSE), \S16.5.1.1 (QSE designation), \S16.11.1, \S16.11.3 and \S16.11.4.3.2 (financial security). Accessed 22 and 30 August 2026; \S3 text read and per-section effective dates checked 14 September 2026; \S2 Block Load Transfer and \S9.17.1 read 28 September 2026; \S10.9 read 25 September 2026; \S6.3.2 text read 25 September 2026; \S3.10.7.3, \S6.6, \S10.3.2.3 and \S16.2 read 26 September 2026; \S2 Counter-Party, \S3.1.4.1, \S16.3.1.1 and \S16.11 read 27 September 2026}
